# 12. Business Rules and Financial Integrity

The following rules are mandatory.

## 12.1 No Invented Commercial Values

Do not invent:

- Discount percentages.
- Fixed discount amounts.
- Commission percentages.
- Commission fixed amounts.
- Contractor eligibility requirements.
- Commission conversion conditions.
- Minimum commission amounts.
- Maximum discount limits.
- Payment deadlines.
- Tax treatment.
- Currency.

If business values are unavailable, implement configurable fields and validation without inserting fake production values.

Test fixtures must be clearly identified as test data.

## 12.2 No Duplicate Discounts

The backend must prevent unintended repeated application of the same discount to the same estimate version.

A recalculation must not compound a previously applied discount.

Always calculate from the correct original eligible amount.

## 12.3 No Duplicate Commissions

A lead conversion must not generate multiple commissions accidentally.

Implement a database-backed uniqueness or idempotency strategy based on the approved commission policy and conversion reference.

A legitimate new conversion must remain possible if the business explicitly permits it.

## 12.4 No Self-Approval

A contractor must never approve their own commission.

Only authorized Admin users can approve or reject commissions.

## 12.5 Immutable Financial History

Do not silently rewrite:

- Historical estimates.
- Historical discount applications.
- Approved commission amounts.
- Recorded payment details.
- Reversal records.

Corrections must create traceable history.

## 12.6 Concurrency Protection

The system must handle simultaneous requests safely.

Examples:

- Two requests attempting to consume the last policy usage.
- Two requests attempting to generate the same commission.
- Two Admin actions attempting to approve the same commission.
- Repeated payment-recording requests.

Use database constraints, atomic updates, transactions, or equivalent controls.

