# 19. Acceptance Criteria

Phase 9 is complete only when:

1. Admin can manage discount policies.
2. Admin can configure contractor eligibility.
3. Eligible contractors receive only authorized discounts.
4. Discount calculations are performed by the backend.
5. Discounted estimates preserve original financial values.
6. Admin can manage commission policies.
7. Eligible conversions can generate commission records.
8. Commission calculations follow approved policy rules.
9. Admin can approve or reject commissions.
10. Contractors can view only their own commission records.
11. Payment confirmation can be recorded without automatic transfers.
12. Financial history is preserved.
13. Duplicate discount and commission creation is prevented.
14. Financial actions are audited.
15. Security and ownership isolation tests pass.
16. Existing Phases 3–8 functionality remains operational.
17. Backend tests pass.
18. Frontend lint and production build pass.
19. Database verification passes.
20. Git changes are committed and synchronized.

A feature is not complete merely because its UI exists. The backend, database, authorization, calculations, and tests must all work.

